{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386820-an-elder-asked-about-w20","id":1386820,"title":"An elder asked about W20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T16:57:36-07:00","id":1386820,"title":"An elder asked about W20","content":"Back in the 90s and early aughts, I played and ran Werewolf at length; it was my go-to. <br /> Time passed. The gaming group split up, and those that were left went to other games. I got the pdf of W20, but couldn\u2019t bear to look at it because I would want to play again and feel frustrated with no one to play with.<br /> Tonight, my wife says, \u201cI\u2019d like to play again, maybe Zoom with some folks. Do you know anything about the 20<sup>th</sup> edition?\u201d <br /> So, here I am with all the 2<sup>nd</sup> ed and Rev books on my shelves, and a plethora of W20 books beckoning. <br /> <br /> Is the system substantively different? Is there enough content change/improvement to warrant spending a crapton of cash for the new books?<br /> I expect this has been covered long ago, and if there are threads discussing these, I would be happy to be pointed their way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:19:25-07:00","id":1386827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386820-an-elder-asked-about-w20#post1386820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the system substantively different? Is there enough content change/improvement to warrant spending a crapton of cash for the new books?<br /> I expect this has been covered long ago, and if there are threads discussing these, I would be happy to be pointed their way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 20th Anniversary Edition is a nostalgia edition. We didn't set out to reinvent the wheel. THe system is about 95% identical to what you'd find in the Revised era books, just given a buff and polish. The biggest change you'd probably see on the character sheet is that &quot;Defense&quot; is no longer a separate Ability and has been rolled into Athletics.<br /> <br /> The content of the books, however, are among the best the line has seen, in my most humble of opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:37:52-07:00","id":1386837,"title":"","content":"W20 is, mostly, a flat out improvement. However, it's a fairly incremental improvement. Buying all the W20 books when you have all of 2e and Rev.... well that's going to depend on your budget. If you've got the money to spare? Yeah, it's worth it for a serious WtA fan. The improvements are good, there's a lot of great content, and even books that are direct repeats of older books like Book of the Wyrm, Velvet Shadow, and Rage Across the World don't feel redundant.<br /> <br /> But if money's tight I think you could get back into WtA with the books you have and still have tons of fun.<br /> <br /> Regardless... skip W20 Changing Ways, or at least read it very carefully and be selective with what you include. It's a serious dud in the otherwise top notch W20 line up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:45:52-07:00","id":1386839,"title":"","content":"You'll have no trouble. W20 is, as said above, backwards compatible with previous editions and Werewolf thankfully avoided the sweeping changes that the metaplot made to VtM and MtA. Theres not a W20 book I wouldn't recommend ( except Changing Ways).<br /> <br /> &quot;Have fun storming the Endron building!&quot; - Miracle Max voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:44:50-07:00","id":1386856,"title":"","content":"The only significant places where compatibility is a bit off (not digging through ever Gift anyway) are:<br /> <br /> 1) As noted, Dodge/Defense was folded into Athletics, so any older system that uses Dodge needs to be tweaked (not really hard, if you'd roll Dodge, roll Athletics, if it's a bonus to Dodge, either consider it a bonus to Athletics, or a bonus to Athletics when using it to defend yourself in combat).<br /> <br /> 2) W20 changed how Tribal Background Restrictions work by having two categories: Discouraged (can't use your starting Background dots on them, but can get them with Freebies or during play), and Restriction (can't have them at all). This has an impact on Tribal culture (Resources is Discouraged for Bone Gnawers, meaning Bone Gnawers are actually capable of having money now), and makes a bunch of Revised Merits that were basically, &quot;get the equivalent of 1 dot in a Background you're not allowed t have,&quot; obsolete.<br /> <br /> 3) W20 uses a more clear presentation of Totems (first introduced in Dark Ages: Werewolf), so updating older Totems will require some judgement calls on what's an individual trait and what's a pack trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T18:48:22-07:00","id":1386859,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the comments, folks. This is helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T19:17:39-07:00","id":1386865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386820-an-elder-asked-about-w20?p=1386837#post1386837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 is, mostly, a flat out improvement. However, it's a fairly incremental improvement. Buying all the W20 books when you have all of 2e and Rev.... well that's going to depend on your budget. If you've got the money to spare? Yeah, it's worth it for a serious WtA fan. The improvements are good, there's a lot of great content, and even books that are direct repeats of older books like Book of the Wyrm, Velvet Shadow, and Rage Across the World don't feel redundant.<br /> <br /> But if money's tight I think you could get back into WtA with the books you have and still have tons of fun.<br /> <br /> Regardless... skip W20 Changing Ways, or at least read it very carefully and be selective with what you include. It's a serious dud in the otherwise top notch W20 line up.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this. Though I would also avoid Shattered Dreams as well. Its layout and structure is really awkward at times. There are a couple of gems in there - the War of Shame entry is great. <br /> <br /> But all you really need is W20. Its a giant book, filled with a lot of great material. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T07:45:48-07:00","id":1387492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386820-an-elder-asked-about-w20?p=1386827#post1386827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 20th Anniversary Edition is a nostalgia edition. We didn't set out to reinvent the wheel. The system is about 95% identical to what you'd find in the Revised era books, just given a buff and polish. The biggest change you'd probably see on the character sheet is that &quot;Defense&quot; is no longer a separate Ability and has been rolled into Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Ian, I've to disagree here.<br /> While some passages are even 100% copy and paste from revised, there are some substantial changes in W20. And while V20 provided sidebars and explanations, W20 lacked this.<br /> <br /> From the top of my head:<ul><li>In contrast to revised Edition FAQ pre-change Garou are now considered kinfolk. Discerning the two with &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; isn't possible any more (despite 'Baptism of fire' stating otherwise (being copy and past)). How grave the implications of this are, is for everyone to decide themselves.</li> <li>Sidestepping changed back to 2nd Edition prerequisites, specifically a mirror-like surface. Even going so far as to stating that mobile mirrors are at increased difficulty. This is a huge step away from revised editions ability to step sideways basically anywhere.</li> <li>W20 has Gifts and Rites, some of which are newly added and never before were in a Werewolf publication. It doesn't however compile all Gifts or Rites from previous books. V20, in my opinion, did a better work to compile previously available information. As did the 20th Anniversary editions of Changeling and Wraith.</li> </ul><br /> W20 certainly is a nice book, but it also is kinda expensive. But, unlike V5 there wasn't an all to big overhaul of the game mechanics. So, if you already own revised edition......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T22:19:15-07:00","id":1387650,"title":"","content":"For me I am finding it harder and harder to justify any of the 20th edition books over revised. Yes there are some changes but I don\u2019t think they justify buying, what I don\u2019t really conceder, a new edition of the game and for the most part regret spending money on them only because I already owned all the revised books. This is just my opinion but I would rather of just kept playing Revised. If you don\u2019t own revised already though I would recommend 20th as it is easy to buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 05-12-2020, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}